meta {
  name: Cancel Request
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/portal/requests/{{portalRequestId}}/cancel
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Origin: {{portalOrigin}}
  X-CSRF-Token: {{portalCsrfToken}}
}

body:json {
  {}
}

docs {
  Requires the server to run with `ENABLE_SELF_SERVE=true` ("Mis citas" is off by default: every
  /portal path answers 404) and a `portal_session` cookie. No login issues that cookie now that the
  codes are gone, so this request only works against a session minted for a future login.

  Cancels one of the session email's pending booking requests (approval mode). A booking request
  to cancel must exist (Confirm Booking on a `REQUIRE_APPROVAL` provider); `portalRequestId` is set by hand. Needs the
  session cookie, the exact Origin and the CSRF token. The body is an empty object (or none).

  204 on success: the request becomes CANCELLED and its slot is released. Every other case (not
  theirs, another provider's, unknown, already resolved, expired) is the same 404 "Request not
  found". It works even while booking is paused.
}
